Focused BGP argument regression
===============================

t_ctlargs.c and test.h come from smytht's unit-test contribution,
yellowman/nsh PR #179, commit 01877f0418715cb17738359c0b879c80713eef8e.
Only this witness is included here; the broader suite and makeargv fix
remain separate. The four BGP KNOWN_BUG checks are now CHECKs.

On OpenBSD:
    make -f Makefile.ctlargs test

The BGP and OSPF table copies must track bgpcommands.c and commands.c.
Additional checks cover all optional prefixes through the final slot,
one excess word, required arguments, abbreviation/ambiguity, and the
leading NULL slots used by ctl handlers. Output includes expected parser
error messages from rejection checks.
